Assuming that you (Derek), as a gentoo user, compiled it yourself, how did
you compile, install and start it? 

Did you do "make" and "make install" (the latter as root) in the main
source directory (the one where there are subdirectories dat, doc,
include, src, sys, util and win) as it should be done or something else?
Oh, and before that, did you read the file sys/install/Install.unx?

Did you start it with the nethack script that goes to the /usr/games
directory (as should be done) or directly from the binary file in
/usr/games/lib/nethackdir (unless you changed the directory name) or
something else?

> > user/group. Is Nethack supposed to be usable by two people playing
> > their own characters at the same time in separate worlds?

Certainly yes.

> You *are* playing each person under a different account right? that *is*
> required. It won't work if everyone logs in under the same account no
> matter what. 

Actually, it IS possible to start two different Nethack games on the same
user account, I remember having accidentally done it. You just can't save
both of them.

